1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,401
Surprise surprise I did not find anything except this sun hat for my boyfriend.
毫不意外，除了给男朋友找到这顶遮阳帽，我什么都没淘到。

2
00:00:04,401 --> 00:00:06,081
Or I guess I did find a couple items.
或者说，我倒也找到过几件东西。

3
00:00:06,081 --> 00:00:09,271
But I was not about to spend 18 on a princess polly dress.
但我不打算花18买一条 Princess Polly 的连衣裙。

4
00:00:09,281 --> 00:00:15,440
One because it's polyester two they don't even have changing rooms so I can't even try on the dress.
第一，它是涤纶的；第二，店里连试衣间都没有，所以我根本没办法试。

5
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:19,120
And then that other one was so cute it gave me 1920 s flapper vibes.
另一条很可爱，给人一种1920年代摩登女郎裙的感觉。

6
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:23,841
But 40 this is a thrift store.
但要40？这里可是旧衣店啊。

7
00:00:23,841 --> 00:00:25,281
I don't know it's just ridiculous.
我不知道，真的很离谱。

8
00:00:25,281 --> 00:00:30,961
And I feel like whenever I talk about how hard it is to thrift while plus size I understand that this is a universal issue.
每次聊到大码淘衣有多难，我也明白，找不到合适衣服是很多人共有的问题。

9
00:00:30,961 --> 00:00:36,880
And it's harder for people of smaller sizes to find cute stuff at thrift stores for a reasonable price too.
身形更小的人，也很难在旧衣店以合理价格找到好看的衣服。

10
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,961
And there's a lot of different factors at play.
这背后有很多不同因素在起作用。

11
00:00:38,961 --> 00:00:44,391
But my point being is that every time I talk about trying to find clothes as a plus sized person.
但我的重点是：每次谈到自己作为大码人士寻找衣服时……

12
00:00:44,401 --> 00:00:49,031
Usually people say well if you can't find new clothes just go thrifting.
别人通常会说，买不到新衣服，那就去淘二手的呀。

13
00:00:49,041 --> 00:00:53,601
And then when you go thrifting and you can't find items that make you feel good or fit you.
等你去淘衣，却找不到穿着感觉好、或者真正合身的衣服时……

14
00:00:53,601 --> 00:00:56,391
It's well why don't you learn how to make your own clothes then.
他们又说，那你为什么不学着自己做衣服呢？

15
00:00:56,401 --> 00:00:58,071
Or maybe you should lose weight then.
或者说，那你也许应该减肥。

16
00:00:58,081 --> 00:01:02,161
And it's just ridiculous like why would I ever change my body to fit into clothes.
这真的很荒唐：我为什么要为了塞进衣服而改变自己的身体？

17
00:01:02,161 --> 00:01:05,110
Clothes are supposed to fit us they're supposed to fit our bodies.
衣服应该适合我们，应该适合我们的身体。

18
00:01:05,120 --> 00:01:08,081
We're not supposed to alter our bodies to fit into clothes.
我们不应该为了穿进衣服而改变自己的身体。

19
00:01:08,081 --> 00:01:11,601
I just feel like people don't understand or like hear themselves when they say that.
我只是觉得，别人说这种话时，可能没明白自己在说什么，也没听清自己的话。

20
00:01:11,601 --> 00:01:14,081
And how ridiculous of an argument that is.
那样的论点实在很荒唐。

21
00:01:14,081 --> 00:01:17,110
I don't know I'm trying to debate if I should go to one more thrift store.
我不知道，还在犹豫要不要再去一家旧衣店。

22
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:23,361
Mostly because I feel defeated in my soul so I feel like even if I do go I'm not going to find anything.
主要是我心里已经很挫败，感觉就算再去，也淘不到什么。

23
00:01:23,361 --> 00:01:30,430
But on the other hand I am a very very very very stubborn human being.
但另一方面，我又是一个非常、非常、非常、非常固执的人。

24
00:01:30,440 --> 00:01:33,361
H yeah let's go to another thrift store.
嗯，好吧，再去一家旧衣店。

25
00:01:33,361 --> 00:01:37,440
Last one though okay because my soul cannot handle going to seven or eight thrift stores.
不过这是最后一家，我的心真的承受不了逛七八家旧衣店。

26
00:01:37,440 --> 00:01:43,441
I just cannot handle that right now.
我现在真的承受不了。

27
00:02:31,601 --> 00:02:38,320
And that's when I decided to give up and call it a day.
于是我决定放弃，今天就到这里。

28
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:42,081
It's haul time baby one item does not a whole make.
到分享战利品的时候啦！只有一件，实在算不上一次完整的战利品分享。

29
00:02:42,081 --> 00:02:46,320
So I decided to include some items that I found over the past few weeks.
所以我也加上了过去几周找到的一些东西。

30
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:52,401
Or that I've gotten from plus size vintage sellers so let's just jump right in.
还有从大码古着卖家那里买的东西，那我们直接开始吧。

31
00:02:52,401 --> 00:02:56,880
The only item I bought on this thrift trip is this striped top.
这趟淘衣我唯一买下的，就是这件条纹上衣。

32
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:00,961
It's just really cute and basic I've been very into stripes recently.
它很可爱又基础，我最近真的很喜欢条纹。

33
00:03:00,961 --> 00:03:05,360
And I don't know it's 100 cotton it's cute it's nice and lightweight.
我不知道，它是全棉的，可爱、舒服，又轻薄。

34
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:06,791
So it's easy to throw on.
所以随手一穿就可以出门。

35
00:03:06,801 --> 00:03:11,441
And it does have this little detailing on the back of the sleeve little tiered ruffles.
袖子背面还有一点小细节，是层叠的小荷叶边。

36
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:14,880
And I don't know I think there's a lot of different ways to style this.
我觉得它可以搭配出很多不同的样子。

37
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:21,641
And it'll be nice once it's actually hot out because if you live in chicago right now you know the weather has not been feeling very springy.
等天气真正热起来就适合穿了；如果你现在住在芝加哥，就知道这里的天气一点也没有春天的感觉。
